# file-mcp-server Docker Deployment Guide

This guide covers image build, certs, runtime configuration, deployment modes, server control, and Docker-specific tests.

## 1. Build the image

```bash
./docker-build.sh cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

With custom CA for build-time TLS trust:

```bash
CUSTOM_CA_CERT=/path/to/enterprise-ca.crt \
HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.local:3128 \
HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.local:3128 \
./docker-build.sh cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Direct Docker build:

```bash
docker buildx build --load --network=host -t cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest .
```

## 2. Runtime files and mounts

Prepare runtime directories and env:

```bash
mkdir -p run/workspace run/logs certs
cp docker-env.example run/env.base
```

Container mount strategy:
- `run/workspace` -> file scope root and operational storage
- `run/logs` -> audit/server logs and snapshots
- `certs` -> optional CA bundle(s)
- env files -> mounted into `/workspace/*.env`

## 3. Single-config run (host network)

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_CONFIG_PATH=/app/config.yaml \
  -e FILE_MCP_DEFAULTS_PATH=/app/defaults.yaml \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Health check:

```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

## 4. Multi-configuration run (layered env files)

`file_mcp_server` supports comma-separated env file paths. Use this to keep base + environment overlays.

Example:

```bash
cat > run/env.prod <<'ENV'
FILE_MCP_API_KEY_PRIMARY=prod-secret
FILE_MCP_ROOT=/workspace
FILE_MCP_AUDIT_LOG=/workspace/logs/audit.log.jsonl
FILE_MCP_SERVER_LOG=/workspace/logs/server.log
FILE_MCP_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/workspace/logs/snapshots
FILE_MCP_HTTP_TRANSPORT=streamable-http
FILE_MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
FILE_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8000
FILE_MCP_HTTP_BASE_PATH=/
FILE_MCP_HTTP_MCP_PATH=/mcp
FILE_MCP_HTTP_HEALTH_PATH=/health
FILE_MCP_HTTP_EVENTS_PATH=/events
FILE_MCP_HTTP_STATELESS=true
FILE_MCP_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=500
ENV
```

```bash
cat > run/env.override <<'ENV'
FILE_MCP_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_S=10
FILE_MCP_CONVERSION_TIMEOUT_S=20
ENV
```

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/logs:/workspace/logs" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.prod:/workspace/env.prod:ro" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.override:/workspace/env.override:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.prod,/workspace/env.override \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

Precedence:
1. OS environment (`docker run -e ...`)
2. Left-to-right env file list (`FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=file1,file2`)
3. `config.yaml`
4. `defaults.yaml`

## 5. Certificate management (CERTS)

Mount a CA bundle and point runtime to it:

```bash
docker run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/workspace:/workspace" \
  -v "$(pwd)/certs:/app/certs:ro" \
  -v "$(pwd)/run/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro" \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  -e FILE_MCP_TLS_CA_BUNDLE=/app/certs/ca.crt \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

The entrypoint installs `FILE_MCP_TLS_CA_BUNDLE` into system trust and exports:
- `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`
- `SSL_CERT_FILE`
- `CURL_CA_BUNDLE`

## 6. Managing and controlling the containerized server

### Foreground (default)

```bash
docker run --rm ... cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

### Lifecycle control using `server_control.sh` in container

```bash
docker run -d --name file-mcp-server ... cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest sleep infinity
```

```bash
docker exec -it file-mcp-server ./server_control.sh \
  --env /workspace/env.base \
  --config /app/config.yaml \
  --defaults /app/defaults.yaml \
  start
```

```bash
docker exec -it file-mcp-server ./server_control.sh \
  --env /workspace/env.base \
  --config /app/config.yaml \
  --defaults /app/defaults.yaml \
  status
```

```bash
docker exec -it file-mcp-server ./server_control.sh \
  --env /workspace/env.base \
  --config /app/config.yaml \
  --defaults /app/defaults.yaml \
  stop
```

## 7. Remote Docker host (optional)

Use the same commands with `-H`:

```bash
docker -H tcp://remote-docker-host:2375 run --rm --name file-mcp-server \
  --network=host \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/workspace:/workspace \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/logs:/workspace/logs \
  -v /srv/file-mcp/env.base:/workspace/env.base:ro \
  -e FILE_MCP_ENV_PATH=/workspace/env.base \
  cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:latest
```

## 8. MCP tools available

Core tools exposed through MCP include:
- File IO: `read_file`, `write_file`, `copy_file`, `move_file`, `move_path`, `rename_path`, `delete_file`, `create_dir`, `chmod_path`, `list_dir`
- Search: `search_paths`, `search_content`
- Diff/Base64: `diff_text`, `diff_files`, `b64_encode`, `b64_decode`, `b64_encode_file`, `b64_decode_to_file`
- Validation: `validate_text`, `validate_file`
- Structured edits: JSON/YAML/XML/HTML/Markdown operations, including `*_file` variants
- Conversion and transactional editing: `convert_file`, `sed_edit_file`

## 9. Deploying to production

1. Build and push image:
```bash
./docker-build.sh registry.example.com/cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:2026.02
```
```bash
docker push registry.example.com/cloud-dog/file-mcp-server:2026.02
```
2. Provision host directories for workspace/logs/certs/env.
3. Run container using host network or published ports.
4. Validate:
```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```
5. Validate authenticated MCP call with client integration test.

## 10. Docker-focused test suite

Run command-only tests (no Docker daemon required):

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
PYTHONPATH=src pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -k command -q
```

Run full Docker integration tests locally (`--network=host` and bridge mode):

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 PYTHONPATH=src \
pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q
```

Enable optional bridge publish validation:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_BRIDGE_TESTS=1 PYTHONPATH=src \
pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q
```

Run against remote Docker host:

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate
FILE_MCP_RUN_DOCKER_TESTS=1 \
FILE_MCP_DOCKER_HOST=tcp://remote-docker-host:2375 \
PYTHONPATH=src pytest tests/test_docker_container_runtime.py -q
```
